   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I would recommend you to plot each panel separately. You can figure out a way to plot truncated bar in ggplot2 (or other specific needs that are not supported in ggtree directly).</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Then you can put them together based on the trick mentioned in <a href=\"https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter7.html#composite_plot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter7.html%23composite_plot&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482135509000&amp;usg=AOvVaw07OnRxVeNZEQLMePPAP-mx\">https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter7.html#composite_plot</a>.</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On Wed, Mar 25, 2020 at 3:27 PM Depin Wang <a href=\"http://mailto:wan...@gmail.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mailto:wan...@gmail.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482135509000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Smin3epputViYxpQMM3iH\">wangde...@gmail.com</a> wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p></div></div>"
